intro='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Assignment 5 | Auto Insights</title><style>'''+css+''' strong{color:#f5f7fa}li{margin:12px 0}img{display:block} </style></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><div class="nav"><a class="brand" href="index.html">AUTO<span>INSIGHTS</span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="index.html">Home</a><a href="assignment4.html">Assignment 4</a><a href="#charts">10 charts</a><a href="#findings">Findings</a></nav></div></header><main id="main"><div class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Assignment 05 · Exploratory Data Analysis</div><h1>Discovering patterns<br><span>in the data.</span></h1><p class="lead">Exploring how vehicle features relate to recorded MSRP, with attention to group differences, missing values, and unusual records.</p><p>Carson Davis · Auto Insights · Applied Data Visualization</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#charts">Explore the charts ↓</a><a class="button secondary" href="#findings">Read five findings</a></div></div><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><b>11,199</b><span>Cleaned records</span></div><div class="stat"><b>10</b><span>Exploratory visualizations</span></div><div class="stat"><b>1990–2017</b><span>Model years</span></div><div class="stat"><b>5</b><span>Research findings</span></div></div><section><h2>Research questions and method</h2><p>How do horsepower and vehicle size relate to recorded MSRP? How does highway fuel economy differ across transmission groups? Do model-year coverage, missing values, or unusual records affect these comparisons?</p><p>I used the cleaned dataset from Assignment 3, which removed 715 exact duplicate records from 11,914 original rows. Each remaining row represents a vehicle specification record, not an individual sale. No further rows were removed globally, no missing values were imputed, and outliers were retained. Each chart documents its own subset. Price analyses retain the source’s dollar values. Fuel-economy comparisons use the existing known non-electric subset.</p><p>Distributions use histograms and box plots. Relationships use scatter plots and Pearson correlations. Group summaries use medians and counts. Model-year patterns are descriptive cross-sectional comparisons. Missing-data rates and review flags identify limitations before final visualizations or modeling.</p></section><section id="charts"><h2>Exploratory visualizations</h2><p>Each chart follows Observation → Interpretation → Research Implication.</p><div class="contents">'''+''.join(f'<a href="#chart{i}">Chart {i:02}</a>' for i in range(1,11))+'''</div></section>'''
end='<section id="findings"><div class="eyebrow">Research connection</div><h2>Five findings for the Results section</h2><ol>'+''.join('<li>'+v+'</li>' for v in findings)+'</ol><h3>What the findings do not establish</h3><p>These are exploratory associations, not causal effects or tests of statistical significance. Records cover selected vehicle specifications rather than a random sample of sales. Multiple trims and model years from the same brand may be related. Recorded MSRP is not a verified current transaction price and is not inflation-adjusted. Group differences may reflect brand, fuel, year, or vehicle-type composition.</p></section><section><h2>Source and reproducibility</h2><p>Cooper Union. <a href="https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/CooperUnion/cardataset">Car Features and MSRP</a>. Kaggle. Data preparation is documented in <a href="assignment3.html">Assignment 3</a>. Related SQL analysis appears in <a href="assignment4.html">Assignment 4</a>.</p><p><a href="data_cleaned.csv" download>Download cleaned data</a> · <a href="build_assignment5.py" download>Download analysis script</a></p><p>Run the Python script beside data_cleaned.csv and assignment4.html with pandas, NumPy, and Matplotlib installed. It regenerates all charts and this page. Chart images are embedded so the page displays even when opened directly.</p></section></main><footer>Carson Davis · Auto Insights · Assignment 5</footer></body></html>'
